{
  "reason": "The current multi-model/expert/stacker pipeline has plateaued at 0.7591 because variance from heterogeneous base learners, tiny coupon experts, and a global stacker/threshold swamps the small real signal in ~8k noisy survey rows; the initial plan correctly diagnoses a variance and inductive-bias mismatch. The most promising place to change is the modeling core: replace the fragile ensemble with a single categorical-native CatBoost that directly learns coupon-conditional heterogeneity, supported by the initial plan's FE fixes and a lower-variance repeated-CV calibrated decision layer. Historical runs confirm native categorical boosting and leakage-safe target statistics help, while adding members without a metric-aligned guard or refitting during predict is the failure mode to avoid.",
  "module": [
    "data_processing_and_feature_engineering",
    "model_design",
    "training_evaluation"
  ],
  "plan": {
    "data_processing_and_feature_engineering": "WHAT: Keep the deterministic ordinal/frequency encoders and CV-safe target encoding, but (a) represent missing venue-frequency values as an explicit 'unknown' category instead of imputing them to 'never', and (b) add composite affinity features: matched_affinity/mean_affinity ratio, affinity × expiration, affinity × direction_same, and a convenience product of distance_level × direction_same × coupon-venue affinity. WHY: missing survey venue rows are systematically different from genuine 'never' responses, and CatBoost cannot synthesize these residual affinity interactions from raw crosses alone; this directly supports the initial plan's single-model shift. HOW: modify CouponFeatureEngineer._build_base to map NaN/empty/None venue entries to 'unknown' before FREQ_MAP lookup, and append the new numeric columns during fit/transform so they are included in numeric_columns and persisted in the bundle; all statistics must still be fit only on training rows, and fit/transform/fit_transform plus CouponFeatureEngineer attribute names must remain compatible.",
    "model_design": "WHAT: Replace the LGBM + CatBoost + EmbMLP + coupon-expert ensemble and context stacker with a single binary CatBoost classifier consuming all raw categoricals plus explicit high-order crosses (coupon × expiration, coupon × direction, coupon × distance_level, coupon × age, coupon × time, coupon × has_children, coupon × income, coupon × gender) as cat_features. WHY: ordered target statistics give a leakage-safe inductive bias for small tabular categorical data with strong group effects, moving coupon-conditional learning inside one model and removing the variance contributors that are keeping validation at 0.7591; this follows the initial plan's systemic replacement while avoiding the historically failed pattern of adding fragile members without a guard. HOW: keep _make_cb, _prepare_cb_frame, and _predict_mlp signatures where possible but remove MLP/expert/stacker training and bundle entries; use moderate CatBoost settings (iterations≈1200, learning_rate≈0.03, depth 6, l2_leaf_reg≈6, thread_count=2, verbose=False) to fit 2 CPU threads/600s, persist the fitted feature engineer, CatBoost model(s), coupon-type thresholds, and label_map under --model, and make run_predict load-only with one forward pass and no refit.",
    "training_evaluation": "WHAT: Replace the single 5-fold OOF and 121-point global threshold sweep with 3×5 repeated stratified CV for lower-variance OOF probabilities, average CatBoost probabilities across repeats/seeds, and use a shrinkage-weighted per-coupon-type threshold where each group threshold is blended toward the global threshold by group count. WHY: an ~8k-row survey dataset makes single-fold threshold estimates noisy, and accuracy is dominated by coupon-conditional base rates; the initial plan requires a decision layer that respects per-coupon heterogeneity without overfitting small subgroups, and historical failures show small-subgroup decisions must be metric-guarded. HOW: inside run_training keep StratifiedKFold(shuffle=True, random_state=42), loop 3 repeats and average OOF probabilities per repeat for global threshold tuning over [0.2,0.8] on plain accuracy; tune per-coupon blended thresholds using only inner training folds so outer OOF remains honest, then refit seed-averaged CatBoost models on full training rows; persist threshold, per-coupon thresholds, label_map, and stack_order-free bundle fields, preserving run_training(data_dir, model_dir), run_predict(data_dir, model_dir, output_path), row_id=0..N-1 input-order output, original-label predictions, and fresh-process load-without-refit behavior."
  }
}
